  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Pragati Arora vs Union Of India & Anr on 29 July, 2025",
    "facts": "By way of the captioned writ petition, the petitioner has challenged an order dated 24.08.2023, by which her services were sought to be terminated by respondent No. 2 - Chief Executive Officer, Food Safety and Standards Authority of India [\"FSSAI\"], and also seeks a direction upon FSSAI to regularise her services. An interim order was passed on 29.08.2023, restraining her termination. 2. By way of the present application, FSSAI seeks vacation of that order.",
    "arguments": "It is contended that, under the protection of the said interim order, the writ petitioner is not attending to her duties and has been unauthorisedly absent for inordinate periods of time. 4. Ms. Jyoti Dutt Sharma, learned counsel for the petitioner, also accepts this position, although the contents of the application are disputed, and she reserves the petitioner's right to contest any disciplinary proceedings that may be instituted against her in accordance with law.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "It is contended that, under the protection of the said interim order, the writ petitioner is not attending to her duties and has been unauthorisedly absent for inordinate periods of time. 4. Ms. Jyoti Dutt Sharma, learned counsel for the petitioner, also accepts this position, although the contents of the application are disputed, and she reserves the petitioner's right to contest any disciplinary proceedings that may be instituted against her in accordance with law.",
